      "side": 1,
      "message": "In FBE, the system update will write the decrypted data of the zip file to blocks and create a /cache/recovery/block.map file and provide it to RECOVERY.\nRECOVERY creates a file by calling MapFile(path) after judging that the index position 0 of the filename array is the \u0027@\u0027 character. The zip file does not need to be decrypted at this point.\nSo SkipDecryption \u003d arg.find(\"@\") \u003d\u003d 1; is a logical error: https://github.com/TeamWin/android_bootable_recovery/blob/701e9abe26353f143287897942e367f8245c6f54/otautil/sysutil.cpp#L191",
